{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1337939-werewolf-timeline-met","id":1337939,"title":"Werewolf Timeline & MET","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-26T00:25:30-07:00","id":1337939,"title":"Werewolf Timeline & MET","content":"Hello,<br /> <br /> I'd like to ask for your oppinion.<br /> <br /> I' became somewhat confused: Currently I've bought the new MET Werewolf. It contains a whole timeline from 2000s to the currendt days.<br /> Caerns fall, Legends die, Stormeater gets banished again...<br /> <br /> How much is it cannon?<br /> <br /> What really bugged me: The &quot;Malady&quot; (thickening Gauntlet caused by global warming) was first introduced in this MET product, but in the Changing Ways pg. 37. clearly includes it as a &quot;Future Fate&quot;.<br /> <br /> So now what?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T01:46:56-07:00","id":1337945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lachdanan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1337939-werewolf-timeline-met#post1337939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much is it cannon?</div> </div> </div> </div>For the tabletop rpg? None.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T04:59:12-07:00","id":1337957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1337939-werewolf-timeline-met?p=1337945#post1337945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the tabletop rpg? None.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's very incomprehensible for me. To licence a game with all of the fluff and let it evolve into/with a totaly distinct storyline &amp; than make a reference to it is... MANDESS!<br /> <br /> I don't say, that it's not true, but disturbing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":562,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","user":"Lachdanan","date":". 09-26-2019, 08:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T05:48:15-07:00","id":1337962,"title":"","content":"You may also notice that Paradox also licensed the IP to a video game maker who is telling their own story, one which doesn\u2019t include Garou with five forms. <br /> <br /> The IP owners licence out the use of the IP in different ways to different companies for different products. Those products are usually adapted to suit the medium in which they work - LARP stuff with MET has different expectations and requirements to what the rpg has to what the video game has. Add into that the MET product was acknowledged as being written along a different path to what we were doing with W20 at the time Paradox subsidiary White Wolf took over shepherding the IP, and in the years that have followed White Wolf has been absorbed back into the parent company and Paradox hasn\u2019t made public what its plans and vision for the world of Werewolf will be. <br /> <br /> In other words, it\u2019s no different to the owners of the Marvel comic characters being comfortable with comics, cartoons, TV shows and cinematic universes working from roughly the same base sources but each building their own divergent ideas and stories along the way. As long as the different expressions of the IP don\u2019t interfere with the message the IP owner wants (or don\u2019t threaten the value of the IP, if the owner doesn\u2019t have their own plan for how they develop it), the owner is in the business of making money. It\u2019s up to them whether they do so by carefully curating different forms to all be compatible and agree with one another, or spread it into different sandboxes where different groups get to play their own way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T06:22:31-07:00","id":1337967,"title":"","content":"By the way it's not bad and have some intresting features and playable.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'll make it into a Mirror Realm and play a little bit with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T08:06:46-07:00","id":1337984,"title":"","content":"Well, Paradox seems not do develop a 5th edition in house again. And, currently no firm has taken that challenge, as far as I know. <br /> <br /> That said, V5 so far has a description of Lupines as antagonists that doesn't give a clue.<br /> Also, BNS's MET version of Werewolf was a collaboration with White Wolf/Paradox's Martin Ericsson.<br /> <br /> So, if a firm ever would make a 5th Edition of Werewolf for the tabletop game, I'd guess there would be some pressure from Paradox/White Wolf to incorporate game mechanics from V5. Also, there there would be some pressure that any licensee would have to go in the way BNS's Werewolf did is also possible, since it fits, kind of, with the radical changes made to Vampire and therefore the WoD setting as a whole. Also, they would consider how much revenue BNS brings to White Wolf as opposed to what a new tabletop edition could bring and use the popularity of the BNS Setting and it's acceptance in LARP games in general as an indicator on how well received the Setting is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}